# Canonical minimal demo.
# Demonstrates:
# - one 1-D ParametricMotionSpace;
# - a self-edge used for repeated generated-clip streaming;
# - full endpoint coverage of the authored scalar axis.
# Does not demonstrate:
# - arbitrary path following or full 2-D steering;
# - dense-family interpolation or zero foot sliding.
#
# Parameter 0 is the wide-curve authored endpoint; parameter 1 is the
# tight-curve authored endpoint. It is normalized authored control, not a
# physical turn-rate unit. Example paths resolve relative to this file.
# Both clips share one skeleton group (see docs/MOTION_CORPUS.md).
node walk 1
registration walk LeftAnkle LeftAnkle,RightAnkle 3 1
example walk 0.0 ../BVH/walkCurve.bvh
example walk 1.0 ../BVH/walkTightCurve.bvh
# Both extremes of the single curvature axis are authored, so the space is
# fully covered. Held to that claim at load.
expect walk spanned_axes 1
expect walk corner_coverage full
edge walk walk
# Raw-sum thresholds calibrated for the D6 metric.
edge_config walk walk 225 250 12 60 7
